  "workload": "Four vCPUs and nominal 4 GiB per VM, same image, four-CPU service quota, 32 downloads and 240 fresh GETs per arm spaced 25 ms apart over six seconds. A is Micropod. B is OrbStack.",
  "method": "Control is the observed Micropod/OrbStack rate ratio in each pair. Replace only the ratio of whole-VMM host CPU-s/wall-s with its common-clean median. Hold each pair's scored bytes per bracket CPU-s and bracket-to-score durations at their measured values. The three factors multiply to the observed ratio. Compare sample standard deviations of log ratios.",
  "limits": "This is an accounting identity using total host VMM CPU across setup, score and drain. A change in service can reflect CPU availability, guest demand, blocking or thread mix. These data do not identify a QoS effect, a kernel bottleneck or an achievable speedup. The two VMM process boundaries differ. Orders alternated. One failed first attempt has a valid bulk rate and remains visible in the all-attempt sensitivity.",
